Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 02:45:58 2026 +0000

    Walk and the compiled checker read exclusion between two declarations with static parameters over the whole parameter type, by existential reduction

    Climb batch 19, rung P (wip/rung-existential-reduction, 612869b4a..8ce9c0ca9), composed from the branch's net change: the P-152 probe's walk.patch and checker.patch, the worker's two changes, and the skeptic's excludesAtMeet, which reads an object type at the meet apart only from a type that neither it nor a supertype of it may be. The team's checker read two declarations as excluding only where its subtyping showed their meet below Bottom, and the team's walk only where one pair of parameter types excluded; the type group's paper of 2011 reads the intersection of two domains that exclude as having "the same extent as Bottom" and gathers the constraint over the whole type, a tuple element by element and every pair of ancestors (Papers/Types/exc-reduction.tick:7-21, Papers/Types/fig-exclusion.tick:55-57, :136-147).

    Folded from the rung's record: FACTS F-258 added, and F-238's and F-252's sentences on row 740 corrected; ledger rows 786 (NEW-P-1, tint, contested), 787 (NEW-P-2), 788 (NEW-P-3) and 789 (NEW-P-4) added, the placeholders numbered in Appendix I, REPORT.md and SKEPTIC.md; the notes on rows 759, 539 and 697 refused for length and on row 159 as closed (the batch record lists them); the internal document's box on exclusion (Specification/appendices/future.tex) given the revised passage's words, with a clause in the entry's Change; PLAN, "Climb batch 19, listed for his review", P.worker.1 and P.skeptic.1. Rows 740 and 741 close after the rungs.

